{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## CORRECTION: 34cd LANDED mid-session; rebased and consolidated\n\nMy earlier comment said 34cd was unpushed. That was true of my base (36e986c188) but went stale\nduring the session: 34cd landed on gerrit/main as e9d4d390c3 (\"34cd: defer autodeploy while a\nreview runs\"). So `voter.in_flight_reviews()` and the autodeploy defer DO now exist on main.\n\nRebased onto gerrit/main (1920dc9fe5) — textually clean, because 34cd touched only the `/health`\nroute in app.py, not the lifespan. Then DROPPED my own reconciler-scoped counter and gated the\ndrain on `voter.in_flight_reviews()` instead, rather than shipping two counters for one fact.\n\nThe gate cannot go stale in either direction: the stop is requested before either wait so no new\nreconciler review can start, and `queue.join()` has already returned so any remaining count is\nthe reconciler's. Had the join timed out instead, a worker review could still be counted — but\nthen the shared budget is spent, so the wait is a no-op.\n\n## Test-fidelity trap this surfaced, worth recording\n\nConsolidating onto voter's counter broke my lifespan tests, because they stubbed\n`review_and_vote` — and `_counting_in_flight` lives INSIDE it, so the count stayed 0 and the gate\nnever fired. The tempting fix (have the stub hold the count itself) would have made the test\nassert against a number it manufactured — the exact \"guard shares the bug's assumption\" shape.\n\nInstead the lifespan tests now slow the GATE (`produce_code_review_verdict`) so the REAL\n`review_and_vote` runs and genuinely holds the count, and completion is read from a vote actually\nbeing cast rather than from a stub's transcript. Relevant because 34cd's\n`test_the_reconciler_path_is_counted_too` is a SOURCE-TEXT assertion (it greps reconcile.py for\n`review_and_vote`), not a behavioural one, so it was too thin to lean on for this gate.\n"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785799549597295001,"uuid":"aa16a183-6744-4c27-8054-f366f11de75a"}